NAME
    tree - print the directory tree

SYNOPSIS
    tree [dir]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints an indented, depth-first listing of everything under the
    current directory (or dir): two spaces of indent per level, a "/"
    after each directory, and a directory's contents right under it.
    Entries come in the order they are stored; "." and ".." are left
    out. "tree: not a directory" when dir is not one. tree is
    /BIN/TREE.

LIMITS
    8 levels: a deeper directory is shown but not entered, and tree
    says "tree: deeper than 8 levels, not all shown" at the end.

EXAMPLES
    tree            from the current directory
    tree /          the whole disk:
                        BIN/
                          AWK
                          ...
                        FRUIT.TXT
                        ...

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: true pre-order (the P8X listed a
    whole level before any subdirectory), an optional start directory,
    no limit of 24 subdirectories per level, and a note when the walk
    stopped short.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/tree.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    dir, find, ls, cd, walk
